%%{init: {"theme": "neutral", "flowchart": {"wrappingWidth": 220}, "sequence": {"wrap": true, "width": 170, "useMaxWidth": false}}}%%
sequenceDiagram
    participant P as perf userspace command
    participant K as Linux perf-events subsystem
    participant H as CPU PMU counter
    participant T as Target thread
    participant B as Kernel ring buffer
    participant A as Offline analyzer

    P->>K: perf_event_open and sampling configuration
    K->>H: Enable event counter and overflow period
    T->>T: Execute normal application instructions
    H->>H: Count cycles or another selected event
    H-->>K: Counter overflow triggers PMU interrupt
    K->>K: Capture CPU, PID, TID, timestamp, and instruction pointer
    K->>K: Capture or reconstruct call-chain data when requested
    K->>B: Write sample and mapping metadata
    P->>B: Read records and write perf.data
    P->>A: Open perf.data with perf report or perf script
    A->>A: Map addresses to DSOs, symbols, source lines, and call paths
